{"requests": [
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "ok so our ADK support agent has like 34 tools now (crm lookups, order stuff, refunds, shipping, a bunch of internal admin ones nobody remembers adding) and gemini keeps calling get_order_status when it should call get_shipment_tracking, or it passes the customer email into order_id. also search_tickets returns the full ticket JSON with every comment thread and it's eating the context after 2-3 calls. demo for the client is thursday. can you look at tools/ and tell me what to rename/merge/trim, and whether I should only expose some of these depending on what the user is asking about?"},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "Question on architecture: I have a root LlmAgent and a separate research sub-agent that does multi-step web lookups. Right now it's in sub_agents=[...] and the root transfers to it, but then the conversation sort of gets stuck there and the user ends up talking to the research agent directly. Should I wrap it as an AgentTool instead? And if so, how should I write its name/description so the root model knows when to call it vs. just answering itself? Also when a tool raises, the model just apologizes and gives up — what should the error string look like so it actually retries with fixed args?"},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "my function tools work fine locally with adk web but once I deploy to Agent Engine every call to the BigQuery tool fails with 403 permission denied. same code. what am I missing??", "needs_instead": "Debugging Cloud deployment credentials/IAM: the Agent Engine service account lacks BigQuery roles. This is a permissions and deployment configuration issue, not a matter of tool design or how the model understands the tools."}
]}
